@startuml use-case-diagram
' HireAssist — Use Case Diagram (UML)
'
' This file is the source of the diagram. use-case-diagram.svg next to it is rendered from it
' and embedded in docs/PROPOSAL.md. After editing, re-render and commit both files together:
'
'   plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/use-case-diagram.puml
'   (or: java -jar plantuml.jar -tsvg docs/diagrams/use-case-diagram.puml)
'
' It must agree with the use cases in docs/PROPOSAL.md. When a use case changes, follow the
' checklist in CLAUDE.md -> "When a use case changes". D-1 is deferred and deliberately absent.

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam actorBorderColor #333333
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam usecaseBorderColor #333333
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #333333
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam arrowColor #333333

' ── People who use the application (left) ─────────────────────────
' A Guest has not signed in. On signing in (UC-0) they act as a Recruiter or an Admin,
' according to their role, so Recruiter and Admin always denote a signed-in user.
actor "Guest" as G
actor "Recruiter" as R
actor "Admin" as AD

' ── Time-driven and indirect actors, who never sign in (right) ────
actor "System Scheduler" as SCH
actor "Candidate" as CD

rectangle "HireAssist" {
  usecase "UC-0\nSign in" as UC0
  usecase "UC-1\nCreate a job opening from\nnatural-language requirements" as UC1
  usecase "UC-2\nBatch-screen resumes\nagainst a job opening" as UC2
  usecase "UC-3\nGenerate candidate-specific\ninterview questions" as UC3
  usecase "UC-4\nMonitor hiring pipeline\nand stale positions" as UC4
  usecase "UC-5\nEnforce candidate\ndata retention" as UC5
  usecase "UC-6\nManage members\nand roles" as UC6
}

' Admin specialises Recruiter: it inherits every Recruiter association (UC-1 to UC-4)
' and adds its own — configuring the retention policy (UC-5) and managing members (UC-6).
R <|- AD

R --- UC1
R --- UC2
R --- UC3
R --- UC4
AD --- UC5
AD --- UC6

' Signing in changes the role a person plays; it is not a kind-of relationship, so no
' generalisation is drawn between Guest and Recruiter or Admin.
G --- UC0

UC4 --- SCH
UC5 --- SCH

' Candidate never signs in; it supplies the resume and consent decision UC-2 processes.
UC2 .. CD

@enduml
